ot verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a> <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></li><li>Wat Na Mueang <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">Stop nearby</span><p>Shophouse No. 53 on Thanon Rat Bamrung in the old market district is a teak house that now operates as a cafe, making it one of the few buildings on this street that visitors can enter and see inside.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siwara Cafe · A teak house on this street ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Opening hours</summary><p>Sundays, 2:00 PM to 8:00 PM</p></details><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>Not verified · Free admission</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Use Rat Bamrung Road into the old town, then connect to Sri Takuapa Road. The walking street section is located around Sri Takuapa and Udomthara Roads.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>Buildings in the old town area preserve traces of Sino-Portuguese or Sino-Takua Pa architecture related to the tin mining era.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Homes and Sino-Portuguese shophouses in the old town, local food, traditional sweets and local snacks, cultural performances, traditional games, and Baba dress</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Database of important archaeological sites in Thailand</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kapook Travel</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/local/537042" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ (Department of Internal Trade, Ministry of Commerce)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A Hundred Stories of Andaman Old Towns</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://anyflip.com/yxwin/sydm/basic/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Manager Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9650000044214" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Manager Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/travel/detail/9650000061422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Research on developing Peranakan cultural tourism routes</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://so04.tci-thaijo.org/index.php/JSTD/article/view/254126" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Kapook Travel</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://travel.kapook.com/view275997.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Postal code for this street not found directly from read sources.</li><li>Verified data on parking, restrooms, wheelchair access, and visit duration not found.</li><li>Facebook page, website, or LINE verified from read sources not found.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>Specific creators of the cultural street not found.</li><li>Evidence that the cultural street itself is registered as a historical site not found; the registration found is for the Takua Pa governor's residence wall.</li><li>Lunar calendar dates for the event not found.</li><li>Direct official image links with verifiable usage rights not found, so photos are omitted.</li><li>Direct evidence that this street was damaged by the 2004 tsunami not verified yet.</li><li>Historical site registration announcement specifying this entire street not found yet.</li><li>Documents specifying the individual founder or responsible person for the street in 2007 not found yet.</li><li>Official announcements for major restoration projects specifically for the street up to 2026 not found yet.</li><li>Old photos with clear usage rights for this street not found yet, so the photos_archive array is empty.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
