/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/governor-wall/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/governor-wall/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/governor-wall/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="Main menu"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/governor-wall/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Switch to dark mode"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Old Buildings & City Traces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Old buildings and city traces</span><h1>Governor’s Residence Wall</h1><p class="english">Governor’s Residence Wall</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">15 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="governor-wall">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/governor-wall.webp" alt="Governor’s Residence Wall" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.830904, 98.366634 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.830904,98.366634" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd>Open every day (hours not specified) <span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd>No admission fee <span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="On this page"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>The governor's camp wall in a tin-mining town by the sea route</h3><p class="era-years">B.E. 2383 to 2424 (1840 to 1881)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Takua Pa Governor's Residence Wall was probably built during the tenure of Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch Na Nakhon), governor of Takua Pa, between 1840 and 1881 (B.E. 2383 to 2424), but academic sources have not established a definite construction year. The wall enclosed the residence and administrative area, serving much like a fortification to protect against danger and provide shelter for townspeople.</p><p>This was the period when Takua Pa grew through its tin-mining economy and coastal trade. The old town lies along the Takua Pa River, which connects to the Andaman Sea and multinational trade networks. Chinese communities involved in mining and trade played an important role, but conflicts over mining interests made a secure protected area necessary. The wall was therefore both the ruler's residence and a means of maintaining order in the town</p><p>The interior layout was divided into the front palace, hall, and rear palace, connected by doorways. It was built with layers of mortar mixed with gravel and sand, on a base wider than the wall itself. The surviving sections are about 5 metres high. Later excavations found Qing-dynasty Chinese ceramics, European ceramics, and contemporary materials, reflecting the town's trade contacts at the time</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานสิ่งแวดล้อมศิลปกรรม (Cultural Environment Office) ONEP: Takua Pa Arts and Cultural Environments</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a lived-in residence to a historical site protected by the old town</h3><p class="era-years">B.E. 2424 to 2568 (1881 to 2025)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>After Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch) left office, the wall and residence continued to be used during the tenure of Phraya Senanuchit (Iam Na Nakhon), from 1881 to 1892 (B.E. 2424 to 2435). King Chulalongkorn visited Takua Pa and viewed the residence on 28 May, R.S. 109, or 1890 (B.E. 2433).</p><p>Later, when the town was relocated to Ko Kho Khao and Ban Yan Yao during the tenure of Phraya Narathipphakdi (Sit Na Nakhon), the former residence lost its official role and was probably abandoned from that period. The verifiable sources found no evidence confirming that the wall was used for another purpose or directly damaged by the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547)</p><p>The Fine Arts Department (Fine Arts Department) registered it as an archaeological monument and defined its land boundary in the Royal Gazette, Volume 113, Special Section 50 Ngor, dated 18 December 1996 (B.E. 2539). It was later cleared and excavated in 1999 (B.E. 2542), followed by restoration and landscaping in later periods. Current sources state that the wall is more stable, but some areas still need care because of weeds and roots</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A living historical site: the old wall becomes Takua Pa's stage</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Today, the Takua Pa Governor's Residence Wall is an archaeological monument open to visitors every day free of charge. An archaeological-site database lists the joint custodians as the Fine Arts Department (Fine Arts Department), Takua Pa Municipality (Takua Pa Municipality), and the Na Nakhon family. The grounds include a lawn and some walkways, with information signs from the Fine Arts Department and the Tourism Authority of Thailand (Tourism Authority of Thailand)</p><p>The site no longer serves as the governor's residence, but remains a landmark in the old town and a venue for ceremonies and community activities. In 2026 (B.E. 2569), Phang Nga Province and Takua Pa Municipality held the event "From Takola to Takua Pa, 12th edition" at the residence from 28 February to 3 March, with performances of khon, Nora and nang talung, religious ceremonies and Buddhist chanting, as well as local food and OTOP products for sale.</p><p>Contemporary use of the site is therefore heritage tourism and learning about life in Takua Pa. At the same time, some sections of the wall remain damaged and have plants growing on them. The verifiable official sources have not announced a new restoration project or specific budget details for 2026 (B.E. 2569)</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <span class="source-offline">National Broadcasting Services of Thailand (National Broadcasting Services of Thailand): From Takola to Takua Pa, 12th edition <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="Timeline · Scroll to explore events"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1840 (B.E. 2383)</p><h3>Began during the time of Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch)</h3><p>It is suggested, not settled, that the construction of the wall surrounding the residence and official area began to defend against enemies and chaos from tin mining conflicts.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1881 (B.E. 2424)</p><h3>The residence was still in use during the next governor's time</h3><p>Phraya Senanuchit (Iam na Nakhon) became the governor, and the use of the residence area continued until 1892, according to documents summarised by the archaeological database.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">28 May R.S. 109</p><h3>King Rama V viewed the governor's residence</h3><p>King Chulalongkorn visited Takua Pa and viewed this governor's residence.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1892 (B.E. 2435)</p><h3>Lost its role when the town centre moved</h3><p>When the town location moved to Ko Khao Island and Ban Yan Yao, the former residence was no longer in use and was likely abandoned from this period.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">18 December 1996 (2539)</p><h3>Registered as a historical site</h3><p>The Fine Arts Department announced its registration and designated the historical area in the Royal Gazette.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1999 (B.E. 2542)</p><h3>Archaeological excavation</h3><p>Qing dynasty Chinese ceramics, European ceramics, pottery fragments, glassware, and architectural decorative pieces were found.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">28 February to 3 March 2026 (B.E. 2569)</p><h3>The residence as an old town event space</h3><p>The 12th 'From Takola to Takua Pa' event was held, featuring performances, ceremonies, and a local food and OTOP goods market.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Ancient wall line</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>See the intact parts of the wall, about 5 meters high, and the sections damaged by time.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Three-part layout</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Observe the division into the front palace, the hall, and the rear palace, complete with connecting doorways.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Construction technique</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Notice the layers of lime mixed with gravel and sand, and the wall's base which is wider than the wall itself.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Information boards</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>There are historical information boards from the Fine Arts Department and the Tourism Authority of Thailand at the front.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Old town context</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located on Udomthara Road on the west bank of the Takua Pa River and near Wat Na Mueang (a local temple).</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2026-02-28 · National Broadcasting Services of Thailand (National Broadcasting Services of Thailand)</p><h3>Phang Nga hosts the 12th 'From Takola to Takua Pa' event</h3><p>Takua Pa Town Municipality organised activities to promote old town tourism at the Takua Pa governor's residence between 28 February and 3 March 2026.</p><span class="source-offline">Read source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The wall has a rectangular layout and its interior is divided into the front palace, the hall, and the rear palace.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>Excavations found both Qing Dynasty Chinese ceramics and European ceramics in the same site.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>From the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, take Rat Bamrung Road, turn right onto Montri 2 Road, then turn left onto Si Takua Pa Road. Go straight for about 260 meters to find the historical site on your left.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance from Phuket was found in the verified sources.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific route or distance from Khao Lak was found in the verified sources.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>No specific departure airport or distance was found in the verified sources.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Wat Na Mueang <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Takua Pa old town market <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Khun In building <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Admission fee</summary><p>No admission fee</p></details><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>From the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, take Rat Bamrung Road, turn right onto Montri 2 Road, then turn left onto Si Takua Pa Road. Go straight for about 260 meters to find the historical site on your left.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The site's archaeological period is estimated at 1840 to 1881 (B.E. 2383 to 2424). It is thought to have been built during the tenure of Phraya Senanuchit (Nuch Na Nakhon), governor of Takua Pa, as a wall around the residence and a defense against enemies.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>See the surviving wall sections, about 5 metres high, and sections damaged over time. Observe the division into the front palace, hall, and rear palace, with connecting doorways, as well as the layers of mortar mixed with gravel and sand and the wall base, which is wider than the wall itself</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Database of Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand: Takua Pa Governor's Residence Wall</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Takua Pa Town · SAC Community Information Center</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1549" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Artistic Heritage Site Worthy of Conservation: Takua Pa</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Database of Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/874" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานสิ่งแวดล้อมศิลปกรรม (Cultural Environment Office) ONEP: Takua Pa Arts and Cultural Environments</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สถานีวิทยุกระจายเสียงแห่งประเทศไทย (Radio Thailand)</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">Open source ↗ <small>Original source offline · checked 8 Sep 2026</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wongnai: Photos of Takua Pa old-town wall</th><td>Blog</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.wongnai.com/attractions/403843FU-%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B3%E0%B9%81%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%87%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B7%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%87%E0%B9%80%E0%B8%81%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%81%E0%B8%B1%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%9B%E0%B9%88%E0%B8%B2/photos/b51c676106884f98a0c8334b8584b456" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>No specific postal code was found in the verified sources.</li><li>Not verified exact opening hours; official sources only state it is open every day.</li><li>No direct phone number, Facebook page, website, or LINE account for the site.</li><li>No verified information on parking fees, restrooms, or accessibility for the elderly or wheelchairs.</li><li>No verified information that the wall is a direct Sino-Portuguese architecture.</li><li>No verified distance or travel time from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport.</li><li>No verified images with usage rights found.</li><li>No verified evidence for an exact starting year of construction, other than the 1840 to 1881 timeframe.</li><li>No verified evidence that the wall was directly affected by the 2004 tsunami.</li><li>No specific restoration project or budget details for 2026.</li><li>No verified old photos with usage rights found.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\phra-narai\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Phra Narai Park · Takuapa attractions · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Rest in the park and continue with town history · Phra Narai Park Takuapa · Takua Pa park · Phang Nga cultural sites"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Phra Narai Park · Takuapa attractions"><meta property="og:description" content="Rest in the park and continue with town history · Phra Narai Park Takuapa · Takua Pa park · Phang Nga cultural sites"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/phra-narai.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Takua Pa 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/phra-narai.png"><meta name="generator" content="Takua Pa 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/phra-narai/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์ ตะกั่วป่า", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "สวนสาธารณะพระนารายณ์", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/phra-narai.webp", "description": "สวนในพื้นที่เทศบาลที่มีเรื่องราวเกี่ยวกับองค์พระนารายณ์", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "หมู่ชุมชนศรีเมือง ถนนเพชรเกษม", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.8696046, "longitude": 98.3445279}, "telephone": "076 421 750"}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อยู่ตรงข้ามสำนักงานเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่าและที่ว่าการเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า บนถนนเพชรเกษม"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "สวนอยู่ภายใต้การดูแลบริหารจัดการของเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า สวนเป็นสถานที่พักผ่อนหย่อนใจและเป็นที่ประดิษฐานองค์เทวรูปพระนารายณ์กับเทพบริวารจำลอง"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ประติมากรรมรูปเคารพพระนารายณ์สำหรับให้ประชาชนสักการะบูชา ภายในสวนมีองค์พระนารายณ์และเทพบริวารจำลองตามข้อมูลแหล่งราชการ พื้นที่ส่วนหนึ่งของสวนจัดเป็นสนามเด็กเล่น"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/phra-narai/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/phra-narai/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="Main menu"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/phra-narai/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Switch to dark mode"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Parks & Public Spaces</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place notes · Parks and public spaces</span><h1>Phra Narai Park</h1><p class="english">Phra Narai Park</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">5 verified items</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="phra-narai">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/phra-narai.webp" alt="Phra Narai Park" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.8696046, 98.3445279 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.8696046,98.3445279" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076 421 750 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="On this page"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#news">News and updates</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>The park's origins remain behind a veil of evidence</h3><p class="era-years"></p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>For Phra Narai Public Park itself, no document has been found stating its construction year, initiator, or reason for establishment. It should therefore not be concluded that the park originated in the tin-mining era or during the period of the town governors merely because Takuapa prospered then.</p><p>What can be confirmed is that the park is in front of Takuapa Town Municipality Office and houses a statue of Phra Narai with replicas of attendant deities. Phra Narai is significant to the town and is used in the municipal emblem, but this evidence explains the significance of the deity and the town, not the park's founding date.</p><p>Takua Pa's context in municipal documents reflects an old town shaped by trade, tin mining, Sino-Portuguese buildings, and a large Chinese community. However, no evidence directly links these elements to the park's construction.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</a> · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>From a sacred space to a town activity stage</h3><p class="era-years">No verifiable timeline has been found.</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The evidence found does not record any transfer of ownership, abandonment, or restoration of the park over time, so it cannot yet be answered whether the park experienced these events. The same applies to the impact of the 2004 tsunami (B.E. 2547), for which no report specifically about this park has been found.</p><p>During the period covered by the available information, the park's role expanded from a place of worship to a public space for the town. It is used for cultural activities, recreation, traditional events, Children's Day events, and as a playground, under the management of Takuapa Town Municipality.</p><p>Old-town documents identify several places and ancient monuments in the municipality, but no Fine Arts Department announcement has been found registering “Phra Narai Park Public Garden” directly as an ancient monument. The park is therefore carefully distinguished from nearby ancient monuments.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://nced.onep.go.th/opendata/2568/oldtown36_announce/takuapa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Old Town boundary delineation project</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A public park in the 2026 context</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The latest publicly available information confirms that the park remains a public space under the care of Takuapa Town Municipality. It contains statues of Phra Narai and attendant deities for worship, as well as a playground and community recreation areas.</p><p>The park also serves as the town's central stage. The Phra Narai worship ceremony and Takua Pa local-products event were held here in 2025 (B.E. 2568), with reports of Takua Pa local-products activities at the park's central stage. The 2023 (B.E. 2566) annual event ran from 27 March to 5 April.</p><p>No official information has been found confirming opening and closing hours, admission fees, the latest physical condition, or a completed construction project. For the proposed “Narai Hub &amp; Commercial Center”, only policy or guidance reports from municipal administrators have been found, so it is not yet considered a completed project.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</a> · <a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Siam Rath</a> · <a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ThaiPR.NET</a> · <a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Naewna</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="Timeline · Scroll to explore events"><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">27 March to 5 April 2023 (B.E. 2566)</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony</h3><p>The annual event is held at Phra Narai Public Park, along with cultural activities and community products.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2025 (2568 BE)</p><h3>Takua Pa good products fair</h3><p>The central stage of the community economic promotion project was held in the park.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2026 (2569 BE)</p><h3>Current status</h3><p>It remains a public park under the municipality's care. It features a worship point, a playground, and an event space.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status unverified">Not verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>The year the park was built has not been found</h3><p>The disclosed documents do not specify the year, founder, or park establishment project.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">Year unspecified</p><h3>Phra Narai statue as a city symbol</h3><p>The municipality document states that the Phra Narai statue is sacred to the townspeople and is used as the municipality seal, but does not specify the year it was enshrined in the park.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Phra Narai and attendant statues</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Replicas of the deities enshrined in the park. The originals are ancient sculptures from the Khao Phra Narai archaeological site, now in the Thalang National Museum.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Municipal symbol</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is used as the emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality, reflecting the town's historical roots linked to Indian culture.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Proximity to the Sunday Market</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The park is a landmark near the Takua Pa Old Town Sunday Market, often used as an activity space or gathering point for festivals.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Event area</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Used for municipal cultural activities, recreation, and local traditional events</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93%E0%B9%8C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="news"><h2>News and updates</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2025-03-14 · ThailandTravel</p><h3>Phra Narai Worship and Takua Pa Good Products Fair 2025 (2568 BE)</h3><p>Announced the event schedule for 14 to 23 March 2025 at the park.</p><a href="https://thailandtravel.app/content/read/3344" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted">2023-03-31 · ThaiPR.NET</p><h3>Phra Narai worship ceremony, an identity of Takua Pa people</h3><p>Reported on the annual event in 2023 (2566 BE), which was held at the park between 27 March and 5 April.</p><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><p class="muted"> · Siam Rath</p><h3>Takua Pa Town Municipality organised community economic promotion activities, Takua Pa good products</h3><p>Used the park's central stage as the area for the 2025 community economic promotion project.</p><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai statues in the park are replicas; the original ancient sculptures were moved for safekeeping at the Thalang National Museum in Phuket.</p><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The Phra Narai image is the official emblem of Takua Pa Town Municipality.</p><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li><a href="/en/places/thung-phra/">Thung Phra Pho Park</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>Located on Si Takua Pa Road, in front of the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, in the old town area.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The park is managed by Takuapa Town Municipality. It is a place for recreation and houses statues of Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities.</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>A Phra Narai devotional sculpture is available for public worship. According to official sources, the park contains Phra Narai and replicas of attendant deities, and part of the park is a playground.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Cultural Information Centre (m-culture)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AAาธารณะอุทยานพระนารายณ์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Phang Nga Primary Educational Service Area Office</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.phangngaedarea.go.th/site/wp-content/uploads/pdf/17225631.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ThaiPR.NET</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thaipr.net/travel/3321904" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">MGR Online</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mgronline.com/south/detail/9550000099132" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sun Khomun Klang Watthanatham (Cultural Information Center)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://m-culture.in.th/album/120992/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%AD%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%97%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%99%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A2%E0%B8%93์" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Siam Rath</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://siamrath.co.th/n/609307" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Naewna</th><td>News</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.naewna.com/lady/892595" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Published and verified opening hours are not verified.</li><li>Admission fee data is not verified.</li><li>Current conditions of facilities like restrooms, parking, and wheelchair accessibility are not verified for 2026.</li><li>The specific schedule for the annual Phra Narai worship ceremony is not confirmed.</li><li>Verified distance from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport not found.</li><li>No information on the construction year or builder has been found.</li><li>No evidence confirming the park's role during the tin-mining era has been found.</li><li>No evidence was found confirming Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture at the garden</li><li>No evidence was found that the garden is registered as an ancient monument</li><li>No nearby places with a verified walking distance were found</li><li>No verified event month or lunar calendar information was found</li><li>The garden's construction year and builder</li><li>The garden's original purpose or founding project</li><li>The history of ownership changes, abandonment, or restoration</li><li>Evidence of impact from the 2004 tsunami ( พ.ศ. 2547 )</li><li>The year the garden itself was registered as an ancient monument</li><li>Opening and closing hours, admission fees, and the latest condition of buildings and structures</li><li>Whether the Narai Hub project is actually underway</li><li>No old image explicitly identified as showing the garden has been found</li><li>No direct URL for a current image file with verifiable usage rights has been found</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\places\riverwalk\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="th" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดท่าน้ำศรีเมือง · ตะกั่วป่า 101</title><meta name="description" content="อาหารและชีวิตริมแม่น้ำ · ตลาดวันเสาร์ตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดตะกั่วป่า · ของกินตะกั่วป่า"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดท่าน้ำศรีเมือง"><meta property="og:description" content="อาหารและชีวิตริมแม่น้ำ · ตลาดวันเสาร์ตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดตะกั่วป่า · ของกินตะกั่วป่า"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/riverwalk.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="th_TH"><meta property="og:site_name" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/riverwalk.png"><meta name="generator" content="ตะกั่วป่า 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า · ตลาดท่าน้ำศรีเมือง", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/riverwalk.webp", "description": "พื้นที่ตลาดริมแม่น้ำที่มีสินค้าและอาหารท้องถิ่น", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า/ถนนริมคลอง ข้างวัดย่านยาว", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "postalCode": "82110", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.87157, "longitude": 98.35091}}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · วันเสาร์ 15:00 ถึง 20:00 น."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · ไม่มีค่าธรรมเนียมการเข้าชม"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "เดินทางไปย่านริมน้ำ/ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า บริเวณข้างวัดย่านยาว; แหล่งข้อมูลระบุว่าสามารถใช้รถรับจ้างท้องถิ่นหรือมอเตอร์ไซค์รับจ้างจากสถานีขนส่งตะกั่วป่าได้"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ตลาดมีชื่อในโครงการตลาดประชารัฐต้องชมว่า ‘ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า ร่วมใจประชารัฐ’ และตั้งอยู่ถนนริมคลองข้างวัดย่านยาว"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "มีแผงจำหน่ายขนมพื้นบ้าน อาหารพื้นเมือง สินค้าโอทอป และของดีเมืองตะกั่วป่า ตลาดตั้งอยู่ติดแนวคลอง/แม่น้ำตะกั่วป่า เหมาะกับการชมวิวริมน้ำและถ่ายภาพ รีวิวผู้ใช้ระบุว่ามีดนตรีสดโดยนักเรียนในบางช่วง"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/riverwalk/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/riverwalk/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">ข้ามไปเนื้อหา</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="ตะกั่วป่า 101 หน้าแรก"><span class="brand-mark">๑๐๑</span><span>ตะกั่วป่า<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/places/" aria-current="page">สถานที่</a><a href="/stories/">เรื่องเล่า</a><a href="/map/">แผนที่</a><a href="/rest/">กินเที่ยว</a><a href="/news/">ความเคลื่อนไหว</a><a href="/trip/">ทริปของคุณ</a><a href="/traditions/" class="nav-more">ประเพณี</a><a href="/eat/" class="nav-more">กินและของฝาก</a><a href="/routes/" class="nav-more">เส้นทางเดิน</a><a href="/leaflet/" class="nav-more">แผ่นพับ</a><a href="/about/" class="nav-more">เกี่ยวกับ</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/places/riverwalk/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="เปิดเมนู"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="ค้นหาในเว็บไซต์ (กด Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/trip/" aria-label="ทริปของคุณ"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/map/">เปิดแผนที่ ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">หน้าแรก</a> / <a href="/places/">สถานที่</a> / ตลาดและของกิน</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">บันทึกสถานที่ · ตลาดและของกิน</span><h1>ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า</h1><p class="english">Takuapa Riverwalk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว 9 ข้อ</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">ตอนนั้น · ก่อนหน้า · ตอนนี้ ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="riverwalk">เพิ่มลงทริป</button><a class="text-link" href="/trip/">ดูทริปของคุณ</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="eager"><figcaption>ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า<small>เครดิต · คลังภาพโครงการกั่วป่าโพ้</small><small>สัญญาอนุญาต · ใช้ในเว็บนี้ได้</small></figcaption></figure></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>ข้อมูลใช้จริง</h2><dl><div><dt>พิกัด</dt><dd>8.87157, 98.35091 <span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.87157,98.35091" target="_blank" rel="noopener">นำทางด้วย Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">แหล่งพิกัด ↗</a></div><div><dt>เวลาเปิด</dt><dd>วันเสาร์ 15:00 ถึง 20:00 น. <span class="fact-status unverified">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>ค่าเข้า</dt><dd>ไม่มีค่าธรรมเนียมการเข้าชม <span class="fact-status unverified">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>ที่จอดรถ</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>ห้องน้ำ</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>รถเข็น</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>การแต่งกาย</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>โทรศัพท์</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>เพจ</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>เว็บไซต์</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><dt>ไลน์</dt><dd><span class="muted">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span></dd></div><div><span class="source-offline">แหล่งข้อมูลการเข้าชม ↗ <small>แหล่งเดิมออฟไลน์ · ตรวจเมื่อ 8 ก.ย. 2569</small></span><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">แหล่งข้อมูลการเข้าชม ↗</a><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">แหล่งข้อมูลการเข้าชม ↗</a><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">แหล่งข้อมูลการเข้าชม ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="สารบัญหน้านี้"><span class="chapter">ในบันทึกหน้านี้</span><a href="#visit">ข้อมูลใช้จริง</a><a href="#eras">ตอนนั้น · ก่อนหน้า · ตอนนี้</a><a href="#timeline">เส้นเวลาแบบจุด</a><a href="#gallery">แกลเลอรี</a><a href="#highlights">จุดเด่นที่ควรดู</a><a href="#did_you_know">รู้หรือไม่</a><a href="#getting_there">วิธีเดินทาง</a><a href="#nearby">ที่ใกล้เคียงและสถานที่ในหมวดเดียวกัน</a><a href="#nearby-note"></a><a href="#faq">คำถามที่พบบ่อย</a><a href="#sources">ที่มาของข้อมูล</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>ตอนนั้น · ก่อนหน้า · ตอนนี้</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">ตอนนั้น</span><h3>จากท่าเรือเมืองเหมือง สู่พื้นที่ตลาดริมน้ำ</h3><p class="era-years">ไม่พบปีสร้างตลาดปัจจุบัน; บริบทเมืองเก่า พ.ศ. 2325 ถึง ต้นพุทธศตวรรษที่ 20</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p>หลักฐานที่มีอธิบายประวัติของพื้นที่เมืองตะกั่วป่าและท่าน้ำ มากกว่าจะระบุวันกำเนิดตลาดริมน้ำแห่งนี้โดยตรง ตะกั่วป่าเป็นเมืองท่าและศูนย์กลางแลกเปลี่ยนสินค้ามาแต่โบราณ ก่อนจะเติบโตจากการขุดแร่ดีบุกและการค้าทางน้ำ เมืองเก่าตั้งอยู่ในทำเลที่มีแม่น้ำล้อมรอบสามด้าน จึงเหมาะทั้งต่อการเดินเรือ การค้า และการป้องกันเมือง</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า<small>เครดิต · คลังภาพโครงการกั่วป่าโพ้</small><small>สัญญาอนุญาต · ใช้ในเว็บนี้ได้</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">แหล่งอ้างอิง · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม</a> · <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร: ชุมชนตลาดใหญ่</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">ก่อนหน้า</span><h3>เมื่อเหมืองซบเซา ท่าน้ำกลายเป็นความทรงจำ แล้วถูกปลุกให้กลับมาคึกคัก</h3><p class="era-years">ราวทศวรรษ 2520 ถึง พ.ศ. 2562</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p>ช่วงหลังจึงเกิดการฟื้นพื้นที่ในรูปตลาดชุมชน ภายใต้ชื่อ “ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า ร่วมใจประชารัฐ” โดยเอกสารกรมการค้าภายในที่จัดทำข้อมูล ณ วันที่ 31 มกราคม 2562 ระบุที่ตั้งข้างวัดย่านยาวและเวลาเปิดวันเสาร์ 15.00 ถึง 20.00 น. ยังไม่พบหลักฐานว่าตลาดได้รับผลกระทบโดยตรงจากสึนามิ พ.ศ. 2547 หรือได้รับการขึ้นทะเบียนโบราณสถานในนามตลาด</p><figure class="research-photo"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"><figcaption>ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า<small>เครดิต · คลังภาพโครงการกั่วป่าโพ้</small><small>สัญญาอนุญาต · ใช้ในเว็บนี้ได้</small></figcaption></figure><div class="era-sources">แหล่งอ้างอิง · <span class="source-offline">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์ <small>แหล่งเดิมออฟไลน์ · ตรวจเมื่อ 8 ก.ย. 2569</small></span> · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">ตอนนี้</span><h3>ตลาดเสาร์ริมคลองที่พาความทรงจำเมืองเก่ากลับมาเดินได้อีกครั้ง</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status unverified">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>ตลาดตั้งอยู่ในภูมิทัศน์เมืองเก่าที่มีอาคารจีนและชิโน-โปรตุกีส กิจกรรมริมแม่น้ำของเทศบาลยังปรากฏในเอกสารแผนงาน เช่น การทำบุญตักบาตรบริเวณริมแม่น้ำข้างวัดนิกรวราราม และกระทรวงวัฒนธรรมมีรายการเทศกาลอาหารทะเลที่ระบุตลาดเป็นสถานที่จัด อย่างไรก็ดี ยังไม่พบชื่อหน่วยงานหรือบุคคลที่ดูแลตลาดโดยตรง รวมถึงโครงการบูรณะถาวรของตัวตลาดในปี 2569</p><div class="era-sources">แหล่งอ้างอิง · <a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gplace</a> · <a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thai-tour</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า: รายงานติดตามแผนพัฒนา</a> · <a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>เส้นเวลาแบบจุด</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="เส้นเวลา เลื่อนเพื่ออ่านเหตุการณ์"><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">พ.ศ. 2352</p><h3>เมืองเดิมถูกพม่าทำลายและผู้คนอพยพ</h3><p>เมืองตะกั่วป่าเดิมถูกทำลายจนร้าง ก่อนมีการฟื้นเมืองบริเวณบ้านตลาดใหญ่ในสมัยรัชกาลที่ 3</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">พ.ศ. 2561</p><h3>ตลาดถูกระบุในโครงการตลาดต้องชม</h3><p>เอกสารภาครัฐระบุชื่อ ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า ร่วมใจประชารัฐ ในจังหวัดพังงา</p><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">ข้อมูล ณ 31 มกราคม 2562</p><h3>มีข้อมูลที่ตั้งและเวลาตลาดอย่างเป็นทางการ</h3><p>กรมการค้าภายในระบุว่าตลาดอยู่ถนนริมคลองข้างวัดย่านยาว เปิดวันเสาร์ 15.00 ถึง 20.00 น.</p><span class="source-offline">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗ <small>แหล่งเดิมออฟไลน์ · ตรวจเมื่อ 8 ก.ย. 2569</small></span></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">ไม่ระบุปี</p><h3>เมืองตะกั่วป่าเติบโตเป็นเมืองท่าและศูนย์กลางการค้า</h3><p>พื้นที่ริมแม่น้ำเป็นแกนของการเดินเรือ แลกเปลี่ยนสินค้า และการตั้งถิ่นฐานของผู้คนหลายชาติ</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">ไม่ระบุปี</p><h3>ย่านจับเสทำหน้าที่เป็นท่าเรือเก่า</h3><p>ชื่อจับเส/จับเซ้เป็นคำจีนฮกเกี้ยนที่หมายถึงท่าเรือ และสัมพันธ์กับชุมชนพ่อค้าจีนกับเศรษฐกิจเหมืองแร่</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">ไม่ระบุปี</p><h3>เหมืองแร่ทยอยปิด เมืองเปลี่ยนจากศูนย์กลางเหมืองสู่เมืองเก่า</h3><p>แหล่งข้อมูลประวัติศาสตร์ท้องถิ่นระบุว่าความรุ่งเรืองจากเหมืองลดลงหลังเหมืองทยอยปิด และแม่น้ำตื้นเขินจากตะกอนเหมือง</p><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p class="era-years">ไม่ระบุปี</p><h3>เทศกาลอาหารทะเลใช้ตลาดเป็นสถานที่จัด</h3><p>ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรมของกระทรวงวัฒนธรรมมีรายการ Takuapa Seafood Festival ณ ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า แต่หน้าที่เปิดได้ไม่แสดงวันที่จัดอย่างชัดเจน</p><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li></ol></section><section class="research-section" id="gallery"><h2>แกลเลอรี</h2><div data-gallery><div class="gallery-tabs" hidden><button type="button" data-tab="today">ภาพวันนี้</button><button type="button" data-tab="archive">ภาพเก่า</button></div><div id="gallery-today" data-panel="today"><h3>ภาพวันนี้</h3><div class="photo-grid"><p class="muted">ยังไม่มีภาพที่ได้รับอนุญาตให้เผยแพร่ในหมวดนี้</p></div></div><div id="gallery-archive" data-panel="archive"><h3>ภาพเก่า</h3><div class="photo-grid"><figure class="research-photo"><a data-lightbox href="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" aria-label="ขยายภาพ · ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า"><img src="/assets/photos/kuapapoh-port.webp" width="264" height="282" alt="ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>ภาพเก่า เรือจอดที่ท่าน้ำตะกั่วป่า<small>เครดิต · คลังภาพโครงการกั่วป่าโพ้</small><small>สัญญาอนุญาต · ใช้ในเว็บนี้ได้</small></figcaption></figure></div></div></div></section><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>จุดเด่นที่ควรดู</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>อาหารและขนมพื้นบ้าน</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>มีแผงจำหน่ายขนมพื้นบ้าน อาหารพื้นเมือง สินค้าโอทอป และของดีเมืองตะกั่วป่า</p><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>บรรยากาศริมคลอง</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>ตลาดตั้งอยู่ติดแนวคลอง/แม่น้ำตะกั่วป่า เหมาะกับการชมวิวริมน้ำและถ่ายภาพ</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>การแสดงและดนตรี</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>รีวิวผู้ใช้ระบุว่ามีดนตรีสดโดยนักเรียนในบางช่วง</p><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>เชื่อมย่านเมืองเก่า</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>อยู่ใกล้ย่านเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่าและอาคารชิโน-โปรตุกีสของชุมชนตลาดใหญ่</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>รู้หรือไม่</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p>คำว่า “จับเส” ที่ใช้เรียกย่านการค้าเก่า สัมพันธ์กับคำจีนฮกเกี้ยนและท่าเรือเก่าของตะกั่วป่า</p><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">ยืนยันแล้ว</span><p>เมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่ามีหลักฐานการค้าทางน้ำกับเรือสินค้าจากจีนและพม่า</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>วิธีเดินทาง</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>ตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่า</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>เดินทางไปย่านริมน้ำ/ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า บริเวณข้างวัดย่านยาว; แหล่งข้อมูลระบุว่าสามารถใช้รถรับจ้างท้องถิ่นหรือมอเตอร์ไซค์รับจ้างจากสถานีขนส่งตะกั่วป่าได้</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>ภูเก็ต</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>ไม่พบเส้นทางหรือระยะทางเฉพาะตลาดจากแหล่งที่อ่านได้</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>เขาหลัก</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>ไม่พบเส้นทางหรือระยะทางเฉพาะตลาดจากแหล่งที่อ่านได้</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>สนามบิน</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span><p>ไม่พบเส้นทางหรือระยะทางเฉพาะตลาดจากแหล่งที่อ่านได้</p><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>ที่ใกล้เคียงและสถานที่ในหมวดเดียวกัน</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>วัดย่านยาว (วัดนิกรวราราม) <span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span> <span class="source-offline">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗ <small>แหล่งเดิมออฟไลน์ · ตรวจเมื่อ 8 ก.ย. 2569</small></span></li><li>ย่านเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า/ชุมชนตลาดใหญ่ <span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span> <a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li>สถานีขนส่งตะกั่วป่า <span class="fact-status unknown">ยังไม่ยืนยัน</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">อ่านแหล่งอ้างอิง ↗</a></li><li><a href="/places/culture-street/">ถนนสายวัฒนธรรมเมืองเก่าตะกั่วป่า</a></li><li><a href="/places/food-center/">ศูนย์อาหารลานโล่งตะกั่วป่า</a></li></ul></section><aside class="nearby-note"><span class="chapter">แวะพักใกล้ ๆ</span><p>ถ้าเดินตลาดเสร็จแล้วอยากนั่งพัก ย่านตลาดเก่าอยู่ห่างไปไม่ไกล มีบ้านไม้เก่าที่เปิดเป็นคาเฟ่อยู่ริมถนนราษฎร์บำรุง</p><a class="text-link" href="https://siwaracafe.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ที่นั่งพักใกล้ตลาด ↗</a></aside><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>คำถามที่พบบ่อย</h2><details><summary>เปิดให้เข้าชมเวลาใด</summary><p>ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · วันเสาร์ 15:00 ถึง 20:00 น.</p></details><details><summary>มีค่าเข้าชมหรือไม่</summary><p>ข้อมูลยังไม่ยืนยัน · ไม่มีค่าธรรมเนียมการเข้าชม</p></details><details><summary>เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร</summary><p>เดินทางไปย่านริมน้ำ/ถนนศรีตะกั่วป่า บริเวณข้างวัดย่านยาว; แหล่งข้อมูลระบุว่าสามารถใช้รถรับจ้างท้องถิ่นหรือมอเตอร์ไซค์รับจ้างจากสถานีขนส่งตะกั่วป่าได้</p></details><details><summary>สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร</summary><p>ตลาดมีชื่อในโครงการตลาดประชารัฐต้องชมว่า ‘ตลาดริมน้ำตะกั่วป่า ร่วมใจประชารัฐ’ และตั้งอยู่ถนนริมคลองข้างวัดย่านยาว</p></details><details><summary>มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม</summary><p>มีแผงจำหน่ายขนมพื้นบ้าน อาหารพื้นเมือง สินค้าโอทอป และของดีเมืองตะกั่วป่า ตลาดตั้งอยู่ติดแนวคลอง/แม่น้ำตะกั่วป่า เหมาะกับการชมวิวริมน้ำและถ่ายภาพ รีวิวผู้ใช้ระบุว่ามีดนตรีสดโดยนักเรียนในบางช่วง</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>ที่มาของข้อมูล</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>ชื่อ</th><th>ประเภท</th><th>วันที่เข้าถึง</th><th>ลิงก์</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">กรมการค้าภายใน กระทรวงพาณิชย์</th><td>หน่วยงานทางการ</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><span class="source-offline">เปิดแหล่ง ↗ <small>แหล่งเดิมออฟไลน์ · ตรวจเมื่อ 8 ก.ย. 2569</small></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta (ข้อมูล OpenStreetMap)</th><td>แหล่งข้อมูลอื่น</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/W816145865" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thai-tour</th><td>บล็อก</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.thai-tour.com/place/phangnga/takuapa/4206" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Gplace</th><td>บล็อก</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.gplace.com/960259" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ศูนย์มานุษยวิทยาสิรินธร: ชุมชนตลาดใหญ่</th><td>แหล่งข้อมูลอื่น</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wikicommunity.sac.or.th/community/1527" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม</th><td>หน่วยงานทางการ</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/index.php/site/detail/4431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Wanderlog</th><td>แหล่งข้อมูลอื่น</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://wanderlog.com/place/details/11412806/takuapa-river-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">สำนักงานนโยบายและแผนทรัพยากรธรรมชาติและสิ่งแวดล้อม</th><td>หน่วยงานทางการ</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4428" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า</th><td>หน่วยงานทางการ</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_strategy/2022-12_231dcd9d5169573.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">ปฏิทินวัฒนธรรม กระทรวงวัฒนธรรม</th><td>หน่วยงานทางการ</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://calendar.m-culture.go.th/events/103651" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Muang Boran Journal</th><td>บล็อก</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.muangboranjournal.com/post/Takuapa_Naver_Ending_Stories" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">กระทรวงพาณิชย์: ตลาดต้องชมภาคใต้</th><td>หน่วยงานทางการ</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://einspection.moc.go.th/th/file/get/file/20210720dcb8f52155b576a7ca523b2a2247e871134559.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เปิดแหล่ง ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>ข้อมูลที่ยังหาไม่เจอ</summary><ul><li>ไม่พบพิกัดที่ติดป้ายชื่อเฉพาะตลาดริมน้ำ จึงใช้พิกัดตลาด/พื้นที่ใกล้เคียงจาก OpenStreetMap ผ่าน Mapcarta</li><li>ไม่พบเบอร์โทรศัพท์ เพจเฟซบุ๊ก เว็บไซต์ หรือ LINE ทางการของตลาด</li><li>ไม่พบหลักฐานยืนยันปีสร้าง ผู้สร้าง หรือการขึ้นทะเบียนโบราณสถานของตลาด</li><li>ไม่พบข้อมูลยืนยันที่จอดรถ ห้องน้ำ การเข้าถึงสำหรับผู้สูงอายุ/รถเข็น และการแต่งกาย</li><li>ไม่พบเทศกาลเฉพาะตลาดที่ยืนยันได้</li><li>ไม่พบลิงก์รูปภาพทางการที่ระบุสิทธิ์การใช้งาน</li><li>ไม่พบหลักฐานระบุปีเปิดตลาดครั้งแรก ผู้ก่อตั้ง ผู้รับผิดชอบ หรือหน่วยงานเจ้าของตลาด</li><li>ไม่พบหลักฐานว่าตลาดถูกทิ้งร้าง บูรณะ หรือเปลี่ยนมือในช่วงใด</li><li>ไม่พบหลักฐานยืนยันผลกระทบโดยตรงจากสึนามิ พ.ศ. 2547 ต่อพื้นที่ตลาด</li><li>ไม่พบหลักฐานว่าตลาดริมน้ำขึ้นทะเบียนโบราณสถาน; การขึ้นทะเบียนที่พบเป็นขององค์ประกอบอื่นในเมืองเก่า</li><li>ไม่พบประกาศเปิดตลาดล่าสุดปี 2569 จากผู้ดูแลโดยตรง จึงยังยืนยันวันเวลาเปิดปัจจุบันไม่ได้</li><li>ไม่พบข่าวย้อนหลัง 5 ปีที่ระบุการบูรณะหรือโครงการพัฒนาตลาดโดยตรงพร้อมวันที่เผยแพร่ชัดเจน</li><li>ไม่พบภาพเก่าที่ระบุว่าเป็นพื้นที่ตลาดริมน้ำโดยตรง</li><li>ภาพทั้งหมดเป็นลิงก์จากแหล่งท่องเที่ยวออนไลน์และไม่ทราบสิทธิ์ ต้องขออนุญาตก่อนใช้</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/" class="footer-name">ตะกั่วป่า <em>101</em></a><p>เมืองหนึ่งเมือง<br>มีเรื่องให้ค่อย ๆ รู้จัก</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="กลับขึ้นด้านบน">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">จัดทำโดยบ้านศิวรา ตะกั่วป่า</a><span>คู่มือเมืองเก่า · จังหวัดพังงา</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">แผ่นพับต้นทาง ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="เมนูด่วน"><a href="/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>หน้าแรก</a><a href="/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>แผนที่</a><a href="/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>กินอะไร</a><a href="/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>ทริป<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
site\en\places\wat-kongkha\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Wat Kongkha Phimuk · Wat Khongkha Takua Pa · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Observing southern ordination hall lines · Khongkha Phimuk Temple · Takua Pa ancient temple · Phang Nga temple"><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Wat Kongkha Phimuk · Wat Khongkha Takua Pa"><meta property="og:description" content="Observing southern ordination hall lines · Khongkha Phimuk Temple · Takua Pa ancient temple · Phang Nga temple"><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-kongkha.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Takua Pa 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/wat-kongkha.png"><meta name="generator" content="Takua Pa 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-kongkha/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "หน้าแรก", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา) · วัดคงคาพิมุข", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "TouristAttraction", "name": "วัดคงคาภิมุข (วัดคงคา)", "url": "https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/", "image": "https://takuapa101.com/assets/wat-kongkha.webp", "description": "มีอุโบสถแบบปักษ์ใต้ซึ่งเอกสารระบุว่าเป็นโบราณสถาน", "address": {"@type": "PostalAddress", "streetAddress": "ถนนราษฎร์บำรุง", "addressLocality": "ตะกั่วป่า", "addressRegion": "พังงา", "addressCountry": "TH"}, "geo": {"@type": "GeoCoordinates", "latitude": 8.840837, "longitude": 98.362899}, "telephone": "076-421-479"}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "เดินทางจากตัวเมืองตะกั่วป่าอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "จากที่ทำการเทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่าไปทางตะวันตกตามถนนเพชรเกษม/ทางหลวงหมายเลข 4 ราว 5 กิโลเมตร เลี้ยวซ้ายเข้าถนนราษฎร์บำรุง ตรงต่อประมาณ 280 เมตร แล้วเลี้ยวซ้ายตามทาง จะพบวัดอยู่ด้านขวามือ"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "สถานที่นี้มีประวัติความเป็นมาอย่างไร", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "อุโบสถและเจดีย์เป็นโบราณสถานที่ยังใช้งานอยู่ และวัดเป็นสถานปฏิบัติธรรมประจำจังหวัดพังงาแห่งที่ 1 กรมศิลปากรประกาศขึ้นทะเบียนโบราณสถานและกำหนดเขตที่ดินในราชกิจจานุเบกษาเมื่อ 18 ธันวาคม พ.ศ. 2539"}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "มีจุดเด่นอะไรให้ชม", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "ชมอาคารก่ออิฐถือปูน หน้าบันและซุ้มประตูหน้าต่างประดับปูนปั้น รวมถึงภาพพระพุทธรูปและลวดลายพันธุ์พฤกษา เป็นหนึ่งในโบราณสถานสำคัญภายในวัดและยังอยู่ในวัดที่มีการใช้งาน วัดตั้งอยู่ริมฝั่งคลองตะกั่วป่าด้านตะวันตก โดยคลองอยู่ทางทิศตะวันออกของวัด"}}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/places/wat-kongkha/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/places/wat-kongkha/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="Main menu"><a href="/en/places/" aria-current="page">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/places/wat-kongkha/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Switch to dark mode"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/en/">Home</a> / <a href="/en/places/">Places</a> / Temples & Pagodas</div><header class="place-hero full-place-hero"><div><span class="chapter">Place record · Temples and pagodas</span><h1>Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</h1><p class="english">Wat Kongkha Phimuk</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">6 items verified</span><p><a class="text-link" href="#eras">Then · Before · Now ↓</a></p><p class="place-hero-actions"><button class="button" type="button" data-trip-add="wat-kongkha">Add to trip</button><a class="text-link" href="/en/trip/">View your trip</a></p></div><div class="place-hero-art"><img src="/assets/wat-kongkha.webp" alt="Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager"></div></header><div class="research-layout"><aside class="visit-card" id="visit"><h2>Practical information</h2><dl><div><dt>Location</dt><dd>8.840837, 98.362899 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div class="directions"><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=8.840837,98.362899" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Navigate with Google Maps ↗</a><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Coordinates source ↗</a></div><div><dt>Opening hours</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Admission fee</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Parking</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Restrooms</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Wheelchair access</dt><dd>OpenStreetMap data via Mapcarta indicates a wheelchair=yes tag, but details on ramp conditions or facilities from official sources are not verified. <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Dress code</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Phone</dt><dd>076-421-479 <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Page</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>Website</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><dt>LINE</dt><dd><span class="muted">Not verified</span></dd></div><div><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visitor information sources ↗</a><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact information ↗</a></div></dl></aside><nav class="research-rail" aria-label="On this page"><span class="chapter">On this page</span><a href="#visit">Practical information</a><a href="#eras">Then · Before · Now</a><a href="#timeline">Dot timeline</a><a href="#highlights">Highlights to see</a><a href="#did_you_know">Did you know</a><a href="#getting_there">Getting there</a><a href="#nearby">Nearby and similar places</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Data Sources</a></nav><div class="research-body"><section class="research-section" id="eras"><h2>Then · Before · Now</h2><div class="era-axis"><article class="era-card" data-era="then"><span class="chapter">Then</span><h3>A riverside temple of Takua Pa, starting under the name 'Wat Kongkha'</h3><p class="era-years">1762 (B.E. 2305) (proposed by local and government sources); 1936 (B.E. 2479) (ordination hall)</p><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p>Evidence from the environmental art agency states the temple was built in 1762 (B.E. 2305) and originally named Wat “Kongkha”, while the archaeological database of Sun Manutsayawitthaya Sirindhorn (Princess Maha Chakri Sirindhorn Anthropology Centre) indicates the age of the important historical site based on the ordination hall built in 1936 (B.E. 2479). The origin should therefore be read as a two-layer history: the temple's age according to registration or accounts, and the age of the surviving buildings, which are not the same.</p><p>The temple is located on an alluvial plain along Khlong Takua Pa, on the west side of the waterway, in a town with a history as a coastal city and a centre for tin mining and maritime trade. This urban context suggests the temple likely served as a religious site for the riverside community. However, no specific evidence for the temple has been found identifying the founder, the reason for construction, or the direct role of Hokkien Chinese or the town governor. Therefore, details beyond the evidence should not be added.</p><p>The ordination hall, built in 1936 (B.E. 2479), is a southern-style brick-and-mortar building facing east, decorated with stucco depicting pagodas, Buddha images, Dharma wheels, and flora. This reflects its role as both a space for religious ceremonies and a showcase of community craftsmanship from the late Rattanakosin period to the reign of King Rama VIII.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4417" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cultural Art Environment (ONEP)</a> · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="before"><span class="chapter">Before</span><h3>A new name, a new historical site, and returning as a living temple</h3><p class="era-years">1940 (B.E. 2483); 1996 (B.E. 2539); 2002 (B.E. 2545)</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The temple history recorded in the archaeological database states that it was originally called Wat Kongkha before being changed to Wat Kongkha Phimuk in 1940 (B.E. 2483). Meanwhile, the ordination hall and pagoda are still in use and have not become ruins isolated from the temple. The different names in documents should be preserved to show readers the site's development.</p><p>Krom Sinlapakon (Fine Arts Department) announced the registration of the ordination hall and pagoda, along with designating the historical site boundaries, in the Royal Gazette on 18 December 1996 (B.E. 2539). The registration ensures the heritage value of the old buildings is protected as an artistic legacy. Concurrently, it remains a private temple affiliated with the Maha Nikaya sect, with resident monks.</p><p>The provincial dharma practice centre registry of Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Haeng Chat (National Office of Buddhism) lists “Kongkha Phimuk” as the 1st dharma practice centre of Phang Nga province according to a 2002 (B.E. 2545) resolution. Currently, the archaeological database indicates that it is maintained and generally in stable condition. However, no evidence has been found verifying if the area was affected by the 2004 (B.E. 2547) tsunami or if it had a specific period of abandonment or restoration.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) Provincial Meditation Center Registry</a></div></article><article class="era-card" data-era="now"><span class="chapter">Now</span><h3>A historical site that still breathes: An active temple and meditation center</h3><p class="era-years">2569 / 2026</p><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>In the latest published information, Wat Kongkha Phimuk still has resident monks and operates as a private temple affiliated with the Maha Nikaya sect. The maintaining agency is stated to be the temple itself, with the archaeological database advising to contact Phra Khru Nanthapanyakon, the abbot, at 076-421-479.</p><p>The ordination hall and pagoda are active historical sites. The temple interior is described as clean, shady, and suitable for religious practices. The temple also serves as the 1st provincial dharma practice centre of Phang Nga, making it a place where people can pay respects to Buddha, admire the stucco work, and engage in dharma practice.</p><p>Activities with cited sources include dharma practice in honour of the monarchy, overnight New Year prayers, Brahmin nun ordination for royal merit, and summer novice ordination. However, no 2026 (B.E. 2569) announcements have been found verifying activity schedules, opening hours, new restoration projects, or facility details. Therefore, you should call the temple before travelling.</p><div class="era-sources">References · <a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</a> · <a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">สำนักงานพระพุทธศาสนาแห่งชาติ (National Office of Buddhism) Provincial Meditation Center Registry</a></div></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="timeline"><h2>Dot timeline</h2><ol class="point-timeline" tabindex="0" aria-label="Timeline · Scroll to explore events"><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">1762 (B.E. 2305)</p><h3>Founding of Wat Kongkha (Data conflicts with building age evidence)</h3><p>ONEP states the temple was built in 1762 and originally named Wat Kongkha, but the archaeological database uses 1936 as the age of the ubosot, so it cannot be concluded whether the site and the building started in the same year.</p><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4417" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">1936 (B.E. 2479)</p><h3>Construction of the ubosot which is an important historical site</h3><p>The rectangular brick and mortar ubosot faces east and features stucco designs and southern Thai style roof structures.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status disputed">Conflicting information</span><p class="era-years">1940 (B.E. 2483)</p><h3>Renamed to Wat Kongkha Phimuk</h3><p>The temple history in the archaeological database states that it was originally named Wat Kongkha and then renamed to Wat Kongkha Phimuk.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">18 December 1996 (2539)</p><h3>Registered as a historical site</h3><p>The Fine Arts Department announced the registration of the historical site and defined the land area in the Royal Gazette Volume 113, Special Part 50 Ngor.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p class="era-years">2002 (B.E. 2545)</p><h3>Became the first provincial meditation practice center of Phang Nga</h3><p>The National Office of Buddhism registry lists Wat Kongkha Phimuk as the first center of Phang Nga province according to resolution 12/2002.</p><a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="missing-photo">No image authorized for publication yet</p><section class="research-section" id="highlights"><h2>Highlights to see</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Historical site ordination hall</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>View the brick and stucco building. The gable and door or window arches are decorated with stucco art, including Buddha images and floral patterns.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Pagoda</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>It is one of the important historical sites within the temple and remains part of the active temple.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Atmosphere along the Takua Pa Canal</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The temple is located on the western bank of the Takua Pa Canal, with the canal situated to the east of the temple.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Stucco details on the gable</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>The front features a pagoda, Buddha images in the gazing and alms-bowl holding postures, while the back features the Dharmachakra and a Naga-protected Buddha.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="did_you_know"><h2>Did you know</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The name 'Kongkha Phimuk' appears as the first entry in the Phang Nga provincial meditation practice center register.</p><a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><span class="fact-status confirmed">Verified</span><p>The ordination hall and pagoda still serve as active historical sites and are not closed off merely as archaeological viewing spots.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="getting_there"><h2>Getting there</h2><div class="research-cards"><article class="research-note"><h3>Takua Pa Town</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span><p>From the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, head west along Phetkasem Road / Highway 4 for about 5 kilometers, turn left onto Rat Bamrung Road, go straight for about 280 meters, then turn left along the path. The temple will be on the right.</p><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Phuket</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Khao Lak</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article><article class="research-note"><h3>Airport</h3><span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span></article></div></section><section class="research-section" id="nearby"><h2>Nearby and similar places</h2><ul class="nearby-links"><li>Somchai Andaman Building <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li>Kanda Supermarket <span class="fact-status unknown">Not verified</span> <a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read source ↗</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a></li><li><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></li></ul></section><section class="research-section" id="faq"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>Getting there from Takua Pa Town</summary><p>From the Takua Pa Town Municipality office, head west along Phetkasem Road / Highway 4 for about 5 kilometers, turn left onto Rat Bamrung Road, go straight for about 280 meters, then turn left along the path. The temple will be on the right.</p></details><details><summary>What is the history of this place?</summary><p>The ordination hall and pagoda are active historical sites, and the temple serves as the first provincial meditation practice center of Phang Nga. The Fine Arts Department (Krom Sinlapakon) announced its registration as a historical site and defined its land boundaries in the Royal Gazette on December 18, 1996 (2539 BE).</p></details><details><summary>What are the highlights to see?</summary><p>Observe the brick and mortar building, with its pediment and arched doors and windows decorated with stucco, including Buddha images and floral patterns. It is one of the important historical sites within the temple and is still in an active temple. The temple is located on the west bank of Khlong Takua Pa, with the canal situated to the east of the temple.</p></details></section><section class="research-section" id="sources"><h2>Data Sources</h2><div class="source-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Date accessed</th><th>Link</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">ฐานข้อมูลแหล่งโบราณคดีที่สำคัญในประเทศไทย (ศมส.) (Important Archaeological Sites in Thailand Database, SAC)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://archaeology.sac.or.th/archaeology/881" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Cultural Art Environment (ONEP)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://culturalenvi.onep.go.th/site/detail/4417" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Mapcarta (Data from OpenStreetMap)</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://mapcarta.com/29028704" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">TAT Media Assets</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://tatmediaassets.com/file/1097442" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Thailand YellowPages</th><td>Other resources</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.yellowpages.co.th/profile/%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%84%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A0%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%A1%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%82-nabHw5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Samnakngan Phraphutthasatsana Haeng Chat (National Office of Buddhism)</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.onab.go.th/th/file/get/file/20230608fc490ca45c00b1249bbe3554a4fdf6fb104517.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">เทศบาลเมืองตะกั่วป่า (Takua Pa Town Municipality) Environmental Operation Plan</th><td>Official agency</td><td>2026-09-07</td><td><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/files/com_news_formdoc/2021-08_35dfd0d7b952500.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open source ↗</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class="unknowns"><summary>Missing data</summary><ul><li>Published and verified opening hours are not verified.</li><li>Admission fee data is not verified.</li><li>Facebook pages, websites, or LINE accounts confirmed to belong to the temple are not verified.</li><li>A postal code verified to match the temple from primary sources is not verified.</li><li>Routes and distances that can be verified from Phuket, Khao Lak, or the airport are not verified.</li><li>Data confirming the temple's role in the tin mining era is not verified.</li><li>Evidence confirming Sino-Portuguese or Chinese architecture is not verified.</li><li>Data confirming parking, restrooms, and recommended visit times are not verified.</li><li>Months or lunar calendar dates for the festivals are not verified.</li><li>Walking times to nearby places are not verified.</li><li>Evidence identifying the founder and reason for construction in 1762 is not verified.</li><li>Sources provide different years for the temple's start and the ordination hall's construction, so the temple's age cannot be summarized into a single year.</li><li>Evidence specifically for the temple regarding its role in tin mining, maritime trade, Hokkien Chinese, or the town ruler system is not verified.</li><li>Evidence confirming it was abandoned or damaged by the 2004 tsunami is not verified.</li><li>News from the past 5 years confirming renovation or development projects specifically for the temple are not verified.</li><li>Old photographs with verifiable sources are not verified.</li><li>A 2026 announcement regarding opening hours, activity schedules, and facilities is not verified.</li></ul></details></section></div></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
